Overall, I like DAoC.  That pretty much sums things up for me.  <BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><LI>I definitly like the group mana/power status display.<BR><LI>Group EXP is TONS! better then solo exp!<BR><LI>Since fatique seems to be important for the melee types, there needs to be a group fatique status display for the tanks though.<BR><LI>The not being able to refresh a buff until after it has faded is annoying to me.<BR><LI>It's nice that (2) 20th lvl Enchanters could be totally different in what they can do.  However; I also find it frustrating with how little information is out there regarding spells and the spell classes.  It's kind of disheartening to think that you could spend 20 lvls "wasting" you time by putting your training points into the wrong casting skill.<BR><LI>8 People in a group!  Div13 night could let Doxx, Lonar or 2 others play with us again.<BR><LI>I think I like the Midgard stuff a tad better..well, I like Medec's class better anyway. So...If we do a DAoC Div13 night...I'd prefer Midgard for our classes.<BR></UL><P>I mostly played the Hyernia Magician Enchanter class up to 8th this weekend and here's my take on this class.  The closest class the enchanter equals in EQ terms is the Magician.<P>1) The pet/solo class.  The pets do well and are very controllable.<BR>2) Their nukes are pretty nice too.<P>Group powers:<BR>1) Pet for extra melee dmg<BR>2) Tank dmg buff seems to do a good job.<BR>3) Nukes seem to get resisted A LOT on mobs that the group get the best exp from.<P>Later in life they get slows, extra dmg buffs and stuns, but totally no mezzing like EQ enchanters.  They get self and pet dmg shields.  The self dmg shields take a ton of mana and seem pretty pointless past 5th or so when you die if you get hit.<P>Summary:  meh,  ALL of the Magician classes have great promise, but unless some better info is given and attention is paid to the Mage ( Eldritch, Enchanter & Mentalist ) I'm thinking DAoC will be a melee + druid + bard game.<P>IOW: I'd avoid playing a Magician based class for now and I plan on switching to Hybernia Verser this week.<P>For the current "best" when it comes to helping you figure out the spell stuff:<P> <A HREF="http://daoc.crgaming.com" TARGET=_blank>http://daoc.crgaming.com</A><P>--------------------<P>Sleethr - 54th DE Mage<BR>Medec - 44th level Battle Cleric<BR>Meekka - 34th DE Rogue<BR>Vowk - 29th Dr00d
